1
00:01:57,666 --> 00:02:00,944
Hey. Aron here, leave a message.
嘿 这是Aron家 有事请留言

2
00:02:01,712 --> 00:02:04,599
Hi Aron, Sonja here... again.
嗨 Aron 又是我... Sonja

3
00:02:04,793 --> 00:02:07,822
I know that you're probably gonna be away this weekend, but...
我知道你这周末可能要出去 但...

4
00:02:07,823 --> 00:02:09,834
listen, think about what we are gonna play.
想想我们要弹什么吧

5
00:02:09,835 --> 00:02:13,888
Please, just we have to decide, we really... we need to practice, OK?
得快点决定下来 我们... 得先排练一下 好吗?

6
00:02:13,923 --> 00:02:16,086
Anyway it will be fun, I promise.
总之 我保证会很有意思的

7
00:02:16,353 --> 00:02:19,699
And... oh, please call mom, please. Because she worries...
还有... 哦 给妈打个电话吧 她总担心...

8
00:02:19,700 --> 00:02:23,157
which you knew already. OK, later A, bye.
你知道的 我不多说了 A 回聊 拜拜

9
00:03:12,700 --> 00:03:15,200
下一个服务站 100英里

10
00:04:10,999 --> 00:04:12,808
Hey. It's Friday night.
嘿 现在是周五晚上

11
00:04:13,485 --> 00:04:16,604
April 25, 2003.
2003年4月25日

12
00:04:16,949 --> 00:04:19,879
I'm just entering Canyonlands.
我刚进入峡谷地国家公园

13
00:04:19,880 --> 00:04:24,668
Just me, the music and the night.
就只有我 听着音乐享受这夜晚

14
00:04:25,266 --> 00:04:27,306
Love it.
爱死了

15
00:05:06,900 --> 00:05:09,200
星期六

16
00:05:52,101 --> 00:05:54,019
Blue John Canyon.
到Blue John峡谷了

17
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:58,320
Guidebook says: 4.5 hours until the Big Drop.
旅行指南上面写: 到Big Drop还要四个半小时

18
00:05:58,688 --> 00:06:01,561
I aim to take 45 minutes off that.
我打算提前45分钟到达

19
00:08:14,648 --> 00:08:16,689
I don't know, I think we should go that way.
不知道 我觉得我们该往那边走

20
00:08:16,789 --> 00:08:18,997
And if we proceed that way, then we need to come back...
我们再往那边走的话 一会还得回来...

21
00:08:22,008 --> 00:08:24,006
You're doing Blue John too, huh?
你们也在Blue John峡谷玩呢?

22
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,548
No, actually, we were headed for the Dome.
不是 我们想去Dome

23
00:08:27,583 --> 00:08:29,607
- But I think we are lost.  - She's lost.
- 但好像迷路了  - 她迷路了

24
00:08:29,608 --> 00:08:31,246
Hang on.
等着

25
00:08:36,844 --> 00:08:38,553
Let's see this.
我看看

26
00:08:39,778 --> 00:08:43,390
- You are... here.  - We are?
- 你们现在... 在这  - 是吗?

27
00:08:43,855 --> 00:08:46,660
I knew that.
我就知道

28
00:08:46,661 --> 00:08:51,062
And the Dome is there.
Dome在那边

29
00:08:53,234 --> 00:08:55,862
I can take you that way if you like.
你们愿意的话 我可以带你们去

30
00:08:57,966 --> 00:09:02,405
Sorry, Friday the 13th there. Not a killer.
不好意思 忘了摘面罩 挺恐怖的吧(《13号星期五》电影中的杀人狂也戴面罩)

31
00:09:03,693 --> 00:09:07,871
I'm only a psychopath on weekdays. It's Saturday, so...
我工作日时才是变态 现在周六 所以...

32
00:09:09,772 --> 00:09:12,727
I can't take this off. It's my face.
这是我的脸 摘不下的

33
00:09:16,405 --> 00:09:18,947
- Aron.  - Kristi.
- 我叫Aron  - 我是Kristi

34
00:09:18,948 --> 00:09:21,736
Allow me to introduce you to my friend Megan.
这是我朋友Megan

35
00:09:22,356 --> 00:09:25,051
- Nice to meet you.  - It's an honor.
- 很高兴认识你  - 很荣幸

36
00:09:25,571 --> 00:09:29,027
What do you say? You're lost, I am the guide, OK?
你们说呢? 你们迷路了 我当你们导游 好吗?

37
00:09:33,031 --> 00:09:35,300
- Why not?  - Sure.
- 有什么关系呢?  - 当然好

38
00:09:35,301 --> 00:09:38,536
All right. This way.
好的 咱们上路了

39
00:09:38,537 --> 00:09:42,933
So you biked from Horseshoe? Is that like 20 miles?
你从Horseshoe那儿骑车来的? 大概有20英里远吧?

40
00:09:42,934 --> 00:09:44,995
17 on the odometer.
里程表上显示的是17英里

41
00:09:45,807 --> 00:09:48,541
Oh, I thought it was 17.2.
我还以为会是17.2英里呢

42
00:09:48,542 --> 00:09:50,914
17.3. Actually.
其实是17.3英里

43
00:09:50,915 --> 00:09:53,300
Ah, You're one of those.
啊 你是那种单车一族吧

44
00:09:53,301 --> 00:09:56,201
- Not one of those.  - Do you spend a lot of time out here?
- 不算是  - 你经常来这吗?

45
00:09:56,884 --> 00:09:58,974
It's my second home.
这儿是我第二个家

46
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:02,527
See? There's the fork right there.
看到了吧? 就是这条岔路

47
00:10:04,779 --> 00:10:07,670
- We totally missed that.  - Glad we bumped into you.
- 我们完全没看见  - 还好碰见你了

48
00:10:08,190 --> 00:10:11,316
- What are the odds considering we're all the way out here?  - Exactly.
- 从这么老远来 能碰见真是太巧了  - 就是啊

49
00:10:11,317 --> 00:10:12,996
You're in the one place in America.
你们在美国某地

50
00:10:13,100 --> 00:10:15,732
You're pretty much guaranteed not to run into a weirdo.
本以为不可能碰见什么怪人的

51
00:10:15,831 --> 00:10:17,885
But what happened?
但你看发生了什么?

52
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:22,868
All right. So the guidebook says...
旅行指南书说...

53
00:10:22,869 --> 00:10:27,047
that the route is through here... but I know a better way.
应该从这穿过去... 但我知道一条更好的路

54
00:10:27,564 --> 00:10:29,945
The cool way.
给力的路

55
00:10:30,355 --> 00:10:34,686
Guaranteed, the best time you can have with your clothes on.
我向你们保证 这肯定会是你们一生中最棒的经历 而无须脱衣

56
00:10:34,687 --> 00:10:37,912
Although, it's better with your clothes off.
当然了 把衣服脱了更好

57
00:10:39,564 --> 00:10:42,352
- It is a bit of a climb.  - We climb.
- 可能需要爬点山  - 我们很能爬的

58
00:10:42,963 --> 00:10:46,082
- And a bit of a squeeze.  - We squeeze.
- 可能会有点挤  - 我们不在乎挤

59
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:52,840
So you get us all the way fucking here 
你把我们一路带到这种烂地儿

60
00:10:52,841 --> 00:10:55,656
and then you tell us you're not a guide...
才告诉我们你不是个导游...

61
00:10:55,656 --> 00:10:58,058
Well no, I'm an engineer.
我不是 我是个工程师

62
00:10:58,059 --> 00:11:00,056
But this is what I really want to do.
但导游才是我的理想职业

63
00:11:00,597 --> 00:11:04,017
That's wonderful. Hey, I... I always wanted to be a supermodel, but...
真棒 我一直想当个超模 但是...

64
00:11:04,018 --> 00:11:06,885
I don't think that's really gonna work, you know?
我不觉得我真能当上

65
00:11:07,345 --> 00:11:09,410
Jesus. What if these things move?
天哪 要是这些东西动了怎么办?

66
00:11:09,600 --> 00:11:12,252
They've been here for millions of years. They're not gonna move.
他们都在这呆了几百万年了 不会动的

67
00:11:12,344 --> 00:11:14,972
- Oh sure they will.  - What?
- 他们当然会动啦  - 什么?

68
00:11:15,668 --> 00:11:19,114
Yeah, everything's moving all the time. Let's just hope not today.
一切都是瞬息万动的 只希望不是今天动喽

69
00:11:19,574 --> 00:11:21,417
Great.
太好了

70
00:11:26,386 --> 00:11:30,520
All right, all you've got to remember, is that everything will be okay.
你们要记住一点 一切都会没事的

71
00:11:31,114 --> 00:11:33,236
Oh, oh my God!
哦 天哪!

72
00:11:36,264 --> 00:11:39,408
Aron, are you okay? Aron?
Aron 你还好吗? Aron?

73
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:41,046
Aron?
Aron呢?

74
00:11:57,012 --> 00:12:01,122
Listen to the guy, he's fine.
听啊 他没事

75
00:12:01,882 --> 00:12:05,236
He is bad shit. You're bad shit!
他太坏了 你这个坏人!

76
00:12:06,516 --> 00:12:09,470
Come on. You've gotta come down here.
快跳吧 快下来看看

77
00:12:09,889 --> 00:12:13,224
- Trust me.  - Trust you? I'll kill you Aron Ralston.
- 相信我  - 相信你? 我要杀了你 Aron Ralston

78
00:12:13,225 --> 00:12:16,155
Oh, please, you love this.
哦 别废话了 你爱冒险的

79
00:12:32,914 --> 00:12:34,626
Nice job!
真不错!

80
00:12:35,070 --> 00:12:38,897
- Megan, you're missing it.  - It's amazing.
- Megan 别错过了  - 很棒的

81
00:12:38,898 --> 00:12:42,598
- Fuck.  - Just jump, Megan.
- 操  - Megan 快跳吧

82
00:12:50,862 --> 00:12:53,834
- Are you okay?  - Nice job.
- 你还好吧?  - 不错啊

83
00:12:56,832 --> 00:12:59,315
- We've got to do it again.  - Again?
- 我们要再跳一次  - 再来?

84
00:12:59,802 --> 00:13:02,298
- Camera.  - Camera.
- 录下来  - 录下来 好的

85
00:13:19,249 --> 00:13:21,239
So, Blue John...
话说 Blue John峡谷...

86
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:26,938
is actually named after this guy Blue John who was Butch Cassidy's cook.
其实是以Butch Cassidy的厨师的名字命名的

87
00:13:27,397 --> 00:13:30,405
From Butch Cassidy and the Sundance Kid.
就是 《虎豹小霸王》(经典西部影片)里的

88
00:13:30,789 --> 00:13:34,383
And they would hide out in these canyons, I guess,
我猜他们曾藏在这些峡谷中

89
00:13:34,384 --> 00:13:38,231
but also what they do is they run horses, wild horses into here 
他们还把野马赶进来

90
00:13:38,232 --> 00:13:40,232
and trap them at the end of the canyon...
把它们困在峡谷底...

91
00:13:40,896 --> 00:13:43,236
and that's how they catch the horses.
以这种方式抓马

92
00:13:43,237 --> 00:13:46,014
- Hey, would you take another picture before I go?  - Yeah.  - OK, cool.
- 嘿 我走之前能和你们再合张影么?  - 当然了  - 那好

93
00:13:46,450 --> 00:13:48,111
Ready?
准备好了么?

94
00:13:49,176 --> 00:13:53,638
One, two, three... Blue John
3 2 1... 于Blue John留念

95
00:13:54,029 --> 00:13:55,589
Will I ever see you again?
我们还能再见吗?

96
00:13:55,900 --> 00:13:57,598
That depends, do you party?
那得看你参不参加聚会了

97
00:13:58,872 --> 00:14:01,514
Do I party? Yes, sometimes.
聚会? 我有时参加

98
00:14:02,040 --> 00:14:04,463
Tomorrow night we're actually, seriously, throwing a party,
明晚 我们还真的要办一个聚会

99
00:14:04,464 --> 00:14:05,200
if you want to come.
你要是愿意 也可以来

100
00:14:05,201 --> 00:14:06,819
Yeah, you should come by to have a beer and kick back.
是啊 过来喝点啤酒 放松一下

101
00:14:07,004 --> 00:14:08,064
OK, where am I going?
好啊 在哪儿?

102
00:14:08,499 --> 00:14:10,675
It's about 20 miles away, near Green River. 
离这儿20英里左右吧 绿河附近

103
00:14:10,676 --> 00:14:12,718
You know the old motel, it's behind that.
你肯定认得那个旧汽车旅馆 就在它后面

104
00:14:12,817 --> 00:14:16,185
There's gonna be a huge inflatable Scooby-Doo. Can't miss it.
到时候那会有个巨大的充气史酷比 你肯定能找到

105
00:14:16,186 --> 00:14:18,148
- Really? Okay. Cool.  - OK.
- 真的吗? 好 很酷  - 好吧

106
00:14:18,999 --> 00:14:22,461
- It's good to meet you. See you.  - Bye.
- 很高兴认识你们 再见  - 拜拜

107
00:14:22,462 --> 00:14:25,464
Scooby-Doo.
是史酷比哦

108
00:14:25,465 --> 00:14:27,895
Yeah. Rock on.
记住了 继续前行

109
00:14:30,694 --> 00:14:33,326
You think he's actually gonna show up?
你觉得他真的会来吗?

110
00:14:33,327 --> 00:14:36,946
I don't think we figured in his day at all.
我们怎么可能预测他的行为

111
00:14:38,295 --> 00:14:40,759
You liked him.
你心动了吧

112
00:18:25,105 --> 00:18:26,916
This is insane.
太他妈操蛋了

113
00:18:50,900 --> 00:18:55,077
Move! This fucking rock.
妈的 石头 快给我动! 

114
00:19:07,065 --> 00:19:08,878
Please.
求你了

115
00:20:09,137 --> 00:20:14,099
Kristi! Megan!
Kristi! Megan! 你们在哪儿!

116
00:20:14,100 --> 00:20:18,088
Kristi! It's Aron!
Kristi! 我是Aron!

117
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,109
Megan!
Megan啊!

118
00:20:51,004 --> 00:20:52,549
Just think.
动动脑子

119
00:23:07,122 --> 00:23:09,596
Fuck.
操

120
00:23:14,200 --> 00:23:16,200
Shit!
妈的!

121
00:24:37,630 --> 00:24:40,043
Sweet.
太好了

122
00:24:56,900 --> 00:24:59,507
Knife's dull.
刀太钝了

123
00:26:38,225 --> 00:26:43,300
星期天

124
00:27:20,392 --> 00:27:24,011
Look at the size of this. How the fuck did this get here?
这石头太他妈大了 它是怎么到这的啊?

125
00:31:31,013 --> 00:31:32,433
Hi, buddy.
嗨 小鬼

126
00:31:32,915 --> 00:31:35,301
Here we go.
我们走咯

127
00:32:22,346 --> 00:32:25,251
It's 03:05.
现在是3点05分

128
00:32:25,252 --> 00:32:30,287
Sunday, April 27, 2003.
2003年4月27日 周日

129
00:32:30,957 --> 00:32:36,163
This marks 24 hours...
我被困在Blue John峡谷里...

130
00:32:36,164 --> 00:32:39,212
of being stuck in Blue John Canyon. 
已经整整一天了

131
00:32:40,200 --> 00:32:44,332
Right where it's just before the Big Drop.
具体方位就在Big Drop前面一点

132
00:32:46,083 --> 00:32:49,447
My name is Aron Ralston. My parents are...
我叫Aron Ralston 我的父母是...

133
00:32:49,448 --> 00:32:50,963
Donna and Larry Ralston.
Donna Ralston和Larry Ralston

134
00:32:50,964 --> 00:32:52,624
From Englewood Colorado.
他们住在Englewood Colorado

135
00:32:55,159 --> 00:33:00,649
Whoever finds this, can keep the recorder...
不管谁找到这个 你可以拿走录像机...

136
00:33:00,650 --> 00:33:05,371
but please try to get in touch with my parents and give them this tape.
但请试着联系我父母 把这盘带子给他们

137
00:33:05,372 --> 00:33:07,499
I would appreciate it.
我会十分感激的

138
00:33:09,202 --> 00:33:13,935
I was descending Blue John yesterday...
我昨天在Blue John峡谷往下走...

139
00:33:14,375 --> 00:33:20,706
when this chalkstone came loose...
这块白垩石突然松动...

140
00:33:20,707 --> 00:33:23,200
and rolled onto my arm.
滚到了我的手臂上

141
00:33:23,201 --> 00:33:25,697
Now it's stuck.
现在它被卡住了

142
00:33:27,042 --> 00:33:31,794
This arm is... has this gray-blue color.
这只手臂... 变成了灰蓝色

143
00:33:32,642 --> 00:33:37,167
It's been without circulation for 24 hours.
其内血液停止流动已经一天

144
00:33:39,438 --> 00:33:42,290
So... I think it's pretty well gone.
所以... 我觉得它差不多已经坏死了

145
00:33:42,910 --> 00:33:46,160
I'm low on food.
我食物快吃完了

146
00:33:47,238 --> 00:33:52,363
That's about 300-400 ml.
这有差不多300到400毫升吧

147
00:33:52,996 --> 00:33:55,278
And that's it for water.
水就剩这么多

148
00:33:58,907 --> 00:34:03,311
I'm in pretty deep doo here.
可以说现在状况很惨淡

149
00:34:07,159 --> 00:34:08,974
Hello?
有人吗?

150
00:34:09,315 --> 00:34:13,027
Please, there's somebody down here.
求你了 有人在下面

151
00:34:13,429 --> 00:34:17,193
Help! I am in the Canyon.
救救我! 我在峡谷里面

152
00:34:56,068 --> 00:34:59,820
Please, help!
求你了 救我!

153
00:35:00,778 --> 00:35:03,008
Help!
救命啊!

154
00:35:03,009 --> 00:35:06,951
Down here. Help!
我在峡谷里 救命啊!

155
00:35:20,354 --> 00:35:22,988
Don't lose it.
别慌

156
00:35:27,940 --> 00:35:30,610
Aron...
Aron 你听着...

157
00:35:32,312 --> 00:35:35,854
Do not lose it.
一定要稳住

158
00:36:26,933 --> 00:36:29,262
Not bad.
还不错嘛

159
00:36:39,016 --> 00:36:41,222
Dinner.
该吃晚饭了

160
00:36:50,424 --> 00:36:53,604
Tomorrow night we're actually, seriously throwing a party, if you want to come.
明天晚上我们真的要办一个聚会 你要是愿意 也可以来

161
00:36:53,605 --> 00:36:55,394
Yeah you should come by to have a beer and kick back.
是啊 过来喝点啤酒 放松一下

162
00:36:55,395 --> 00:36:58,464
There's gonna be a huge inflatable Scooby-Doo.
到时候会有个巨大的充气史酷比

163
00:36:59,113 --> 00:37:01,236
Scooby-Doo.
史酷比

164
00:37:23,605 --> 00:37:25,996
Cold cans.
冻汽水罐

165
00:37:27,942 --> 00:37:30,117
Plastic cup.
塑料杯

166
00:37:32,037 --> 00:37:33,517
Thank you.
谢谢

167
00:37:36,565 --> 00:37:39,199
Can I take a beer?
我能拿瓶啤酒么?

168
00:37:40,424 --> 00:37:42,507
Won't mind if I do.
应该不会介意的吧

169
00:38:43,111 --> 00:38:46,678
Aron here, leave a message.
这是Aron家 有事请留言

170
00:38:49,483 --> 00:38:52,559
Aron, it's mom.
Aron 我是妈妈

171
00:38:52,560 --> 00:38:54,691
I was hoping to catch you.
我想跟你说点事

172
00:38:55,251 --> 00:38:58,188
Are you there? Hello?
你在家吗? 有人吗?

173
00:38:59,823 --> 00:39:03,032
Okay. Nothing urgent.
好吧 也没什么急事

174
00:39:03,752 --> 00:39:06,667
Doug is in New York. So it will be a quiet weekend.
Doug在纽约呢 所以这周末清闲下来了

175
00:39:07,514 --> 00:39:09,744
Call me, OK?
记得回电话 好吗?

176
00:39:29,380 --> 00:39:32,573
- Where are you going?  - Don't know yet.
- 你要去哪?  - 还不知道呢

177
00:39:33,270 --> 00:39:34,565
Right there, Brian.
Brian 我就去这里

178
00:39:35,000 --> 00:39:37,099
Maybe Utah, maybe somewhere else.
也许去犹他州 也许去别的地方

179
00:39:38,002 --> 00:39:41,534
- Have a good one.  - Always do.
- 旅行愉快  - 我会的

180
00:40:09,400 --> 00:40:10,703
Let's go.
开始了

181
00:40:10,704 --> 00:40:14,710
星期一

182
00:42:40,175 --> 00:42:43,411
It's freaking me out looking at myself.
看我自己这个样子太抓狂了

183
00:42:43,937 --> 00:42:46,752
Sorry, hope that's okay.
抱歉 希望你别介意

184
00:42:50,509 --> 00:42:53,250
It's Monday.
现在周一了

185
00:42:55,034 --> 00:42:59,867
Bummer, all day. I tried to set up this pulley.
一整天都很衰 我试着组装一个简易滑轮

186
00:42:59,868 --> 00:43:02,460
All morning. But it did not work.
用了整个上午 还是没用

187
00:43:02,861 --> 00:43:08,283
It was worth a try, but there is too much friction,
值得一试 但摩擦力太大了

188
00:43:08,866 --> 00:43:11,768
it's climbing rope, so there's too much stretch.
这是根攀岩绳 张力太大

189
00:43:12,225 --> 00:43:17,479
What I could use is 20 meters of static rope...
我需要20米长的静力绳(不会或很少伸长的绳子)...

190
00:43:17,480 --> 00:43:20,374
9.8 millimeters.
直径要9.8毫米的

191
00:43:20,399 --> 00:43:26,463
Three or four pulleys, rack of carabiners, a sling, powerdrill...
三四个滑轮 一些吊钩 一根吊索 一个机械钻...

192
00:43:26,464 --> 00:43:29,170
and Pull Kit.
还有一个牵引器

193
00:43:30,048 --> 00:43:34,889
And eight burly men to do the hawling.
再来八个强壮的男人把它拽上去

194
00:43:36,922 --> 00:43:39,969
That should just about do it.
这样就差不多可以了

195
00:43:45,968 --> 00:43:49,541
Another 150ml of water left.
还剩150毫升水

196
00:43:50,815 --> 00:43:55,683
That should keep me alive till tomorrow night.
应该能使我撑到明晚

197
00:43:56,354 --> 00:44:00,215
If I'm lucky. I peeded twice.
前提是我够幸运 我撒了两次尿

198
00:44:00,862 --> 00:44:05,244
Almost pissed my pants.
差点尿到裤子上了

199
00:44:06,591 --> 00:44:09,537
My body's acting really wierd.
身体有点不听使唤

200
00:44:10,170 --> 00:44:14,594
The second time I did it in the CamelBak.
第二次的时候我尿到CamelBak水袋里了

201
00:44:18,152 --> 00:44:20,231
It smells really bad.
太难闻了

202
00:44:22,229 --> 00:44:24,378
But I'm sure it'll settle.
但尿液肯定会变澄清的

203
00:44:26,141 --> 00:44:30,190
It's gotta be chilled, like Sauvignon Blanc.
得放冷一些 就像白索维农(一种白葡萄酒)一样

204
00:44:33,426 --> 00:44:35,579
No number twos.
没有解大手

205
00:44:35,580 --> 00:44:38,801
Which should disappoint my insect friends.
我的昆虫朋友们可要失望了

206
00:44:39,337 --> 00:44:41,082
They'll just have to wait.
它们得再等等

207
00:44:41,736 --> 00:44:44,866
Let's see, what else can I tell you?
我看看 还有什么能说的?

208
00:44:46,662 --> 00:44:51,339
There is this raven that comes every morning.
有只渡鸦每天早上都飞过

209
00:44:55,417 --> 00:44:59,094
I clocked it at 08:17.
我记了下时间 8点17分

210
00:45:01,262 --> 00:45:05,719
I'll film it for you tomorrow.
明天我会拍下它

211
00:45:06,359 --> 00:45:11,293
Every morning at 09:30 I get fifteen minutes of sunlight.
每天早上9点30我能晒到15分钟太阳

212
00:45:11,570 --> 00:45:13,917
It's really nice.
特别舒服

213
00:45:18,491 --> 00:45:22,220
I've been chipping away.
我一直在削这块石头

214
00:45:22,221 --> 00:45:24,892
More to keep warm than anything.
除了保暖 别无他求

215
00:45:26,266 --> 00:45:31,061
I'm beginning to think that my hand is supporting the rock.
我开始想 是我的手在支撑这块石头

216
00:45:31,062 --> 00:45:35,736
So what if I chip away a bit, it actually settles more.
所以有可能我削得越多 手就被压得更紧

217
00:45:42,549 --> 00:45:46,111
I've found this great tourniquet.
我找到了特别适合做止血带的东西

218
00:47:08,265 --> 00:47:11,489
It hasn't been very useful.
没什么用

219
00:47:14,656 --> 00:47:20,648
Listen! Don't buy the cheap made-in-China multitool.
听着! 千万别买便宜的中国刀具

220
00:47:20,891 --> 00:47:24,439
I tried to find my Swiss Army knife, but...
我当初找过我的瑞士军刀 可没找到

221
00:47:25,100 --> 00:47:27,578
This thing came free with a flashlight. 
这东西是买手电筒附赠的

222
00:47:27,579 --> 00:47:29,484
The flashlight was a piece of shit too.
那手电筒也是废物一个

223
00:47:29,930 --> 00:47:32,968
I kept it in my truck for emergencies.
我把它放在车里应急

224
00:47:34,042 --> 00:47:37,400
I don't blame you, Mom.
我不怪你 妈妈

225
00:47:37,401 --> 00:47:43,405
It was a perfectly great stocking stuffer.
这是个很好的圣诞礼物

226
00:47:45,563 --> 00:47:49,921
No way you could have ever known I'd get in this kind of trouble.
你也想不到有一天我会陷入这种麻烦

227
00:47:51,206 --> 00:47:54,140
When we watch this later, the camera has to be turned on?
我们一会看这录像的时候 得先把录像机打开是吗?

228
00:47:54,141 --> 00:47:55,000
- Am I right?  - Yeah.
- 是吗?  - 是的

229
00:47:55,100 --> 00:47:56,485
You have to leave the camera with us 
要是你想让我们看你拍的东西

230
00:47:56,486 --> 00:47:58,249
when we wanna see something that you've made, right?
你就得把录像机留给我们 对吗?

231
00:47:58,249 --> 00:48:01,023
Good job, Hon.
干得好 女儿

232
00:48:04,257 --> 00:48:09,375
- That is really beautiful.  - He's filming her now.
- 真优美  - 他现在在拍她

233
00:48:10,776 --> 00:48:12,481
We can show this?
我们从这能看见?

234
00:48:15,270 --> 00:48:17,885
Go away.
走开啦

235
00:48:18,913 --> 00:48:22,314
We can't just watch it over there.
我们在那就看不见了

236
00:48:26,496 --> 00:48:30,193
Well done.
弹得很棒

237
00:48:33,129 --> 00:48:35,538
Way to go, sis.
加油 妹妹

238
00:48:35,850 --> 00:48:38,384
- Keep playing?  - Yes honey, keep going.
- 还要弹吗?  - 继续吧 宝贝

239
00:50:25,721 --> 00:50:29,606
I love you.
我爱你

240
00:51:06,831 --> 00:51:09,523
So...
那么...

241
00:51:10,311 --> 00:51:13,879
how do I get in?
我怎么进去?

242
00:51:14,728 --> 00:51:18,955
What is the...
那个...

243
00:51:22,013 --> 00:51:25,366
you know, combination?
密码是什么?

244
00:51:27,672 --> 00:51:31,255
If I told you...
我告诉你之前...

245
00:51:31,256 --> 00:51:34,218
I'd have to kill you.
我得先杀了你

246
00:51:34,219 --> 00:51:37,754
But you've already killed me.
可你已经夺走了我的心

247
00:51:49,337 --> 00:51:55,202
Combination? I think I have it.
密码吗? 我知道了

248
00:52:08,764 --> 00:52:09,664
Fuck.
靠

249
00:54:54,042 --> 00:54:56,837
Who's there?
谁啊?

250
00:55:04,200 --> 00:55:05,200
Aron?
Aron吗?

251
00:55:39,701 --> 00:55:43,312
Please.
求你了

252
00:55:55,473 --> 00:55:59,252
Please.
帮帮我

253
00:56:04,396 --> 00:56:10,600
星期二

254
00:56:19,280 --> 00:56:20,532
Good morning, everyone. 
大家早上好

255
00:56:21,000 --> 00:56:25,872
It is seven o'clock here in Canyonlands USA.
现在是早上七点整 我在美国峡谷地国家公园

256
00:56:26,511 --> 00:56:31,411
This morning, on the boulder, we have a very special guest:
今天早上 位于岩石上 我们有位特别嘉宾:

257
00:56:31,412 --> 00:56:35,903
self-proclaimed american superhero...
自称美国超级英雄的...

258
00:56:35,904 --> 00:56:40,998
Aron Ralston. Let's hear it for Aron.
Aron Ralston 欢迎Aron

259
00:56:43,385 --> 00:56:49,374
Goshes! It is a real pleasure to be here. Thank you. Thanks.
天哪! 很荣幸来到这里 谢谢 谢谢大家

260
00:56:50,304 --> 00:56:53,992
Can I say hi to my mom and dad?
我能问候下我爸我妈吗?

261
00:56:53,993 --> 00:56:58,597
Mom and Dad. Mustn't forget Mom and Dad. Right, Aron?
爸妈总是第一位的 Aron 对吧?

262
00:56:58,598 --> 00:57:01,221
Yeah, that's right.
是啊 

263
00:57:01,222 --> 00:57:06,407
Hi mom, I'm really sorry I didn't answer the phone the other night.
嗨 妈妈 真对不起那天晚上没回你电话

264
00:57:06,651 --> 00:57:10,551
If I had, I would have told you where I was going and then...
要是回了 我就会告诉你我要前往何处...

265
00:57:11,170 --> 00:57:15,251
- I probably wouldn't be here right now.  - That's for sure.
- 那我现在也许就不会被卡在这了  - 那是肯定的啦

266
00:57:15,641 --> 00:57:18,036
But like I always say...
但就像我常说的...

267
00:57:18,037 --> 00:57:23,188
Your supreme selfishness is our gain.
你的自私自利是我们快乐的源泉

268
00:57:23,189 --> 00:57:26,225
Thank you, Aron. Anyone else you'd like to say hi to?
谢谢你 Aron 你还想向谁打招呼吗?

269
00:57:26,987 --> 00:57:30,369
- Brian, at work.  - Hi, Aron.
- 我同事Brian  - 嗨 Aron

270
00:57:31,122 --> 00:57:34,434
I probably won't be making it in to work today.
我今天可能上不了班了

271
00:57:35,654 --> 00:57:38,287
Get a load of this guy. Wait. Hold on.
哟 大家快听听 等下 别挂断

272
00:57:38,288 --> 00:57:43,345
We got a question coming in from another Aron...
有个来自犹他州失败者峡谷的Aron...

273
00:57:43,346 --> 00:57:47,373
in Loser Canyon, Utah.
想问你个问题

274
00:57:48,022 --> 00:57:51,277
Aron asks: Am I right in thinking...
他问道: 是不是就算你同事Brian向警方汇报了...

275
00:57:51,278 --> 00:57:56,247
that even if Brian from work notifies the police...
他们也得再等个一天

276
00:57:56,248 --> 00:57:58,543
they'll put a 24-hour hold on it 
才能发一份失踪人口报告出来

277
00:57:58,681 --> 00:58:01,681
before they file a missing persons report?
Aron 是这样吗?

278
00:58:01,681 --> 00:58:06,091
Which means you won't become officially missing...
那么也就是说 最早也得在周三中午之前...

279
00:58:06,092 --> 00:58:10,612
until midday Wednesday at the earliest.
你才算是在案的失踪人口

280
00:58:10,613 --> 00:58:13,680
You're right on the money there, Aron.
是啊 你说到点子上了 Aron

281
00:58:13,681 --> 00:58:18,383
Which means, I'll probably be dead by then.
这意味着 那时候我估计都死了

282
00:58:18,384 --> 00:58:20,872
Aron from Loser Canyon, Utah.
来自犹他州失败者峡谷的Aron

283
00:58:20,873 --> 00:58:24,693
- How do you know so much?  - Well, I will tell you why I know so much.
- 你怎么这么清楚?  - 我来告诉你为什么

284
00:58:25,360 --> 00:58:28,675
I volunteer for a little rescue service.
我当过救援小组的志愿者

285
00:58:29,538 --> 00:58:35,608
You see, I'm something of a, big fucking hard hero.
其实 我算是一个牛逼的英雄人物

286
00:58:36,221 --> 00:58:40,892
I can do everything on my own, you see?
我什么都能自己搞定 看出来了么? 

287
00:58:40,893 --> 00:58:44,054
I do see.
我确实看出来了

288
00:58:45,650 --> 00:58:48,604
Is it true that despite ..
是不是尽管...

289
00:58:49,256 --> 00:58:54,313
or maybe because you're a fucking hard hero...
或者说也许正因为你是个牛逼的英雄人物...

290
00:58:54,314 --> 00:58:57,769
you didn't tell anyone where you were going?
所以你没把你的去向告诉任何人?

291
00:59:00,278 --> 00:59:02,777
Yeah, that's absolutely correct.
是啊 就是这样

292
00:59:05,787 --> 00:59:08,817
- Anyone?  - Anyone.
- 没人知道?  - 没人

293
00:59:11,200 --> 00:59:13,200
Oops.
你悲剧咯

294
00:59:39,155 --> 00:59:42,232
Mom, Dad...
爸 妈...

295
00:59:44,173 --> 00:59:46,740
I just wanna take this time to tell you that, 
我想用剩下的这点时间来告诉你们

296
00:59:47,401 --> 00:59:49,756
the times we've spent together were awesome...
我们在一起的那些日子很美好...

297
00:59:51,956 --> 00:59:55,795
and I haven't appreciated you in my heart as I know that I could.
我却没有全心全意去珍惜它们

298
00:59:58,057 --> 01:00:01,459
Mom, I love you...
妈 我爱你...

299
01:00:01,460 --> 01:00:04,508
and I wish I had returned all your calls...
我真希望我每次都给你回电话了...

300
01:00:04,509 --> 01:00:06,652
Ever.
每一次

301
01:00:09,215 --> 01:00:13,231
I love you guys.
我爱你们

302
01:00:13,970 --> 01:00:17,265
And I'll always be with you.
我会一生一世在你们身边

303
01:02:28,927 --> 01:02:36,358
Wednesday
星期三

304
01:03:10,693 --> 01:03:13,043
This is no Slurpy.
一点都不像思乐冰(一种碳酸饮料)

305
01:03:15,978 --> 01:03:18,572
It's like a bag of piss.
喝起来就是一包尿

306
01:03:53,922 --> 01:03:55,884
OK, I'm gonna go up again.
我再上去一次

307
01:03:58,430 --> 01:04:00,306
Great one.
真棒

308
01:04:00,600 --> 01:04:04,200
- Listen.  - We can tell you more. OK.
- 听着  - 我们再告诉你件事 

309
01:04:04,300 --> 01:04:06,048
- Tell him.  - We are very worried about you.
- 快说  - 我们很担心你

310
01:04:07,055 --> 01:04:10,260
- We're worried about your music.  - An advice for your choice of music.
- 我们对你的音乐品位表示担忧  - 给你个选择音乐的小建议

311
01:04:10,261 --> 01:04:12,356
If you keeps singing "Fish Are Really Rock"...
要是你还继续唱 "Fish Are Really Rock" 这首歌...

312
01:04:12,357 --> 01:04:14,074
then you never get a girlfriend.
你就永远找不到女朋友了

313
01:04:14,074 --> 01:04:15,991
- Never.  - You may have one but I really doubt it.
- 永远找不到  - 也许能有一个 不过我对此表示怀疑

314
01:04:15,992 --> 01:04:17,623
You're maybe sort of cute.
你挺可爱的

315
01:04:17,623 --> 01:04:19,380
- Occationally.  - Occationally.
- 有时候了  - 只是有时候

316
01:04:20,310 --> 01:04:22,816
OK, this cannon ball is for you.
好了 给你表演个抱膝跳水

317
01:04:32,405 --> 01:04:39,104
I'm going to test your theory about whether or not it's better...
我准备验证一下你的理论...

318
01:04:39,413 --> 01:04:41,920
with or without clothes on.
看看到底是穿上衣服还是脱了衣服好

319
01:05:08,734 --> 01:05:12,288
Don't.
别

320
01:05:12,289 --> 01:05:16,656
Please, don't.
千万要忍住

321
01:05:18,752 --> 01:05:22,346
- Don't.  - Ralston, rock on.
- 忍住  - Ralston 你真牛

322
01:07:16,736 --> 01:07:20,169
You don't even want me here, do you?
你都不想让我呆在这了 是吗?

323
01:07:22,109 --> 01:07:24,751
I'm gonna go, Aron.
我要走了 Aron

324
01:07:27,003 --> 01:07:29,408
Is that what you want?
这就是你想要的吧?

325
01:07:32,432 --> 01:07:34,881
It is, isn't it?
就是这样吧?

326
01:07:37,700 --> 01:07:38,200
Okay.
那好

327
01:07:41,961 --> 01:07:44,268
Come back.
回来啊

328
01:07:47,876 --> 01:07:50,113
You're gonna be so lonely, Aron.
Aron 你会无比孤单的

329
01:08:06,844 --> 01:08:10,953
46, 47, 48, 49...
四十六 四十七 四十八 四十九...

330
01:08:10,954 --> 01:08:14,944
50! And here I am! I'm coming.
五十! 我要来了!

331
01:08:18,553 --> 01:08:20,260
I'm holding on.
我还在坚持

332
01:08:21,743 --> 01:08:24,582
Time's moving really slowly.
时间过得太慢了

333
01:08:25,365 --> 01:08:31,931
My heart's beating really fast. I swear to God, it feels like it...
我的心脏跳得特别快 我向上帝发誓 感觉它的...

334
01:08:31,932 --> 01:08:34,714
it's beating three times as fast as it should be.
速度是正常时候的三倍

335
01:08:40,641 --> 01:08:44,730
So cold.
我很冷

336
01:08:50,501 --> 01:08:51,702
Blue John?
你是Blue John吗?

337
01:08:56,671 --> 01:09:01,611
I love you.
我爱你

338
01:09:03,909 --> 01:09:09,208
Rana, I've been thinking about you, girl.
Rana 我一直在想你

339
01:09:15,139 --> 01:09:19,052
I know how I am. I've tried to do everything. Whatever it was...
我知道自己现在状态很差 我什么都试过了 任何方法...

340
01:09:19,053 --> 01:09:23,211
- I tried.  - Aron, where are you?
- 我都试过了  - Aron 你在哪呢?

341
01:09:36,083 --> 01:09:40,022
What are you guys doing here? Andy.
你们怎么在这? Andy

342
01:09:40,668 --> 01:09:43,959
Tom. Hi, guys. What's going on?
Tom 你们好啊 怎么了? 

343
01:09:45,200 --> 01:09:47,632
- Aron.  - Hey.
- Aron  - 嘿

344
01:09:50,107 --> 01:09:53,195
You look like the Hole in the Wall Gang.
你们看起来就像 "Hole in the Wall Gang" (北爱尔兰喜剧小组)的成员

345
01:09:55,566 --> 01:09:57,565
Dorks.
一群傻瓜

346
01:10:00,032 --> 01:10:02,248
Found you Aron.
找到你了 Aron

347
01:10:08,967 --> 01:10:13,287
Sis, I'm sorry that I won't be at your wedding.
妹妹 对不起 我不能参加你的婚礼了

348
01:10:13,288 --> 01:10:15,712
I know that I promised to play.
我知道我保证过要弹钢琴的

349
01:10:15,713 --> 01:10:18,102
That we play.
是我们一起弹

350
01:10:18,103 --> 01:10:21,766
I'm sorry. I know it'll be a good one.
对不起 婚礼一定会很完美的

351
01:10:23,845 --> 01:10:28,223
8:15, there's no raven. 8:20...
八点一刻了 渡鸦还没来 八点二十了...

352
01:10:28,686 --> 01:10:31,990
I think that my raven didn't come.
我觉得那只渡鸦不会来了

353
01:10:36,029 --> 01:10:38,335
I've been thinking.
我一直在想

354
01:10:38,336 --> 01:10:41,663
Everything...
所有事...

355
01:10:41,664 --> 01:10:45,060
- just comes together.  - You're gonna be so lonely, Aron.
- 都集中到一起了  - Aron 你会无比孤单的

356
01:10:45,067 --> 01:10:47,148
- Have a good one.  - Always do.
- 旅行愉快  - 我会的

357
01:10:47,149 --> 01:10:49,590
- Later!  - It' me.
- 回见!  - 是我

358
01:10:49,591 --> 01:10:51,289
Aron, it's mom.
Aron 我是妈妈

359
01:10:51,290 --> 01:10:53,703
- I was hoping to catch you.  - I chose this.
- 我想和你说点事  - 是我自己导致的

360
01:10:53,704 --> 01:10:55,863
Doug is in New York. So it'll be a quiet weekend.
Doug在纽约呢 所以这周末清闲下来了

361
01:10:55,864 --> 01:10:58,968
- I chose all of this.  - Call me.
- 是我自己导致了这一切  - 记得回电话

362
01:11:02,787 --> 01:11:05,231
This rock...
这块石头...

363
01:11:05,876 --> 01:11:09,163
this rock has been waiting for me my entire life.
这块石头足足等了我一辈子

364
01:11:09,820 --> 01:11:12,613
I hate this rock!
我恨这块石头!

365
01:11:13,721 --> 01:11:18,067
And its entire life. Ever since it was a bit of meteorite.
从它还是一丁点的陨石开始 它便用尽一生来等待我

366
01:11:18,268 --> 01:11:19,740
A million billion years ago.
从一千万亿年之前就开始了

367
01:11:19,900 --> 01:11:21,250
How the fuck did this get here?
这他妈的怎么到这来的?

368
01:11:21,251 --> 01:11:24,466
There in space. It's been waiting...
从宇宙中来 它就等待着...

369
01:11:26,081 --> 01:11:28,323
to come here.
来到这里

370
01:11:28,324 --> 01:11:31,327
Right, right here.
这个地方 这个位置

371
01:11:33,889 --> 01:11:37,741
I've been moving towards it my whole life. The minute I was born.
我的一生都在朝它走来 从我出生的那一刻起

372
01:11:38,177 --> 01:11:41,547
Every breath I've taken, every action...
我的每次呼吸 所做的每件事...

373
01:11:41,548 --> 01:11:46,755
has been leading me to this. A crack on the earth surface.
都在引领我来这儿 这个地缝里

374
01:16:01,839 --> 01:16:04,039
Come on.
坚持住

375
01:16:38,259 --> 01:16:40,827
Don't pass out.
别晕过去

376
01:19:41,203 --> 01:19:42,529
Thank you.
谢谢这一切

377
01:21:50,967 --> 01:21:52,861
Easy.
放轻松

378
01:21:58,324 --> 01:22:02,013
Easy. Come on.
放轻松 没事的

379
01:25:33,636 --> 01:25:35,754
Help me.
救救我

380
01:25:40,972 --> 01:25:43,796
I need help.
救命啊

381
01:25:54,981 --> 01:26:02,149
I need some water. I was stuck in a crack.
我要喝水 我被卡在岩缝里了

382
01:26:02,695 --> 01:26:07,705
Some water, please. I cut my arm off.
给我点水 求你了 我截断了我的手臂

383
01:26:10,153 --> 01:26:13,169
Please, some water.
求你了 给我点水

384
01:26:14,919 --> 01:26:16,683
Thank you.
谢谢

385
01:26:25,615 --> 01:26:28,615
- Do you have a phone?  - Yes, but no signal.
- 你带电话了吗?  - 带了 但是没信号

386
01:26:29,153 --> 01:26:32,554
- You should stop and rest.  - No.
- 你该停下来歇歇  - 不用

387
01:26:32,555 --> 01:26:34,135
I better keep going.
我得继续走

388
01:26:34,962 --> 01:26:38,410
Will you run? Will you run ahead?
你们跑吧 往前跑好吗?

389
01:28:49,980 --> 01:28:52,802
Aron's premonition came true.
预兆成为了现实

390
01:28:54,386 --> 01:28:57,536
He met his wife Jessica three years later.
3年后Aron遇见了他的妻子Jessica

391
01:28:59,500 --> 01:29:03,600
Their son, Leo, was born in February 2010.
2010年2月份 他们的儿子Leo出生了

392
01:29:07,630 --> 01:29:11,311
Aron continued to be a climber and canyoneer.
Aron继续他的攀登和峡谷冒险事业

393
01:29:18,476 --> 01:29:24,000
He always leaves a note to say where he has gone.
不同的是 他总会留个便条告诉家人他去哪了

394
